  *   LEVEL                "the robot is upright now" (recapture tilt reference)
  *   RESET                clear a tip-over latch (refused while still tipped)
  *   GESTURES             -> "OK wave point ..."
+ *   WALK <n>             walk n crank steps (+ forward, - back, 1..50) -> "OK <est_ms>"
+ *   TURN <deg>           turn in place, multiple of 30 (+ = left/CCW, |deg| <= 720)
+ *                        -> "OK <est_ms>". Completion shows in STATUS (walk=idle,
+ *                        walk_last=DONE_R_90 / ABORT_W_1_stall, walk_seq=N).
+ *                        Refused while tipped, bumped or already walking.
+ *   CAL                  -> "OK ms=<l>,<r> deg=<deg/step> mode=<1|0> yawsign=<1|-1>"
+ *   CAL MS <0|1|2> <ms>  ms per crank step, side 0=L 1=R 2=both (Uno EEPROM)
+ *   CAL DEG <deg>        degrees turned per turn step (Uno EEPROM)
+ *   CAL MODE <1|0>       1 = count crank switches, 0 = timed fallback
+ *   CAL COUNTS           Uno prints its switch counts (shows in the server log)
+ *   CAL YAWSIGN <1|-1>   iPhone yaw direction (+1: yaw grows turning left)
  *   PING                 -> "OK PONG" (also feeds the watchdog)
  *   STATUS               -> "OK <l> <r> <ms_since_cmd> <dist_m> <estop> key=val..."
  *   SIM T|B|READY [n]    stub backend only: inject a co-processor event (tests)
  *
+ * iPhone yaw (optional, -y <udp_port>): datagrams "YAW <deg>" (see
+ * laptop/iphone_yaw_bridge.py). After a TURN finishes, if yaw is fresh, the
+ * server measures the real turn and sends up to 2 raw correction steps.
+ *
  * Threads:
  *   main      accept loop, one detached thread per client
+ *   yaw       (with -y) receives iPhone yaw datagrams, stores them under lock
  *   control   SCHED_RR high priority, fixed-rate tick. The ONLY thread that
  *             talks to the backend: drains events (tip/bump/ready), applies
  *             the watchdog / obstacle / tip / bump stops, slews the wheels,
  *             plays gesture keyframes and keeps a model of the arm angles.
  *
  * Usage: tars_motor [-b uno|stub|pico] [-d dev] [-p port] [-w watchdog_ms]
- *                   [-r rt_priority] [-k bump_hold_ms]
+ *                   [-r rt_priority] [-k bump_hold_ms] [-y yaw_udp_port]
  */
